[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. It's a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so you can click either
  the box or the text to toggle it. When it's checked, a few lines of CSS (using [38;5;153m:checked[39m) cross out the text and grey
  it out. There's no JavaScript involved. I haven't opened the page in a browser to check it.

  The task text is a placeholder ("Example task"). To add more items, copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">…</label>[39m block. The
  checked state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. If you want it to stay checked, the next step would be
  storing it in [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m.

  I haven't committed the change.

